ok   set_value stores and reads a scalar
ok   add_list_value builds a list, absent key returns empty array
ok   child! creates and returns a nested Params, nested() never stores
ok   key? is true for scalars, lists and nested params
ok   keys lists scalars, then lists, then nested, each in insertion order
ok   set_path assembles nested params from a Query.split_key-shaped path
ok   require returns the nested Params when present and non-empty
ok   require raises ParameterMissing when absent or empty
ok   permit returns only listed scalar keys that are present
ok   merge! lets the other Params win on conflicts
ok   merge! deep-merges nested Params, keeping receiver-only keys
ok   merge! does not alias other's lists or nested params
ok   merge! preserves keys/inspect ordering: receiver order first, then other's new keys
ok   a name can only be one kind at a time: last write wins, like Rack
ok   to_h returns only scalars, empty? and inspect are deterministic
ok   read_only! marks the Params and every nested child, and returns self
ok   every mutator of a read-only Params raises RuntimeError and changes nothing
ok   every reader of a read-only Params still works
ok   Params.new.merge!(read_only) is writable and independent of its source
ok   read_only! is one flag per tree: a nested node seals its whole tree, copies and strangers are separate
20 tests, 109 assertions, 0 failures
